{
  "_comment": [
    "The pre-arrival SMS send-state, as preSmsState (nala-shared.js) reads it,",
    "and whether the last attempt FAILED, as preSmsFailed reads it. The",
    "phone_cases.json / form_dinner_cases.json pattern: one reader owns the",
    "fact, this table owns the cases, and BOTH suites answer to it - inv_suite",
    "drives arrivals-sms.html, dash_suite drives dashboard.html - so whichever",
    "screen drifts fails by name. The Dashboard's 'to send' count is exactly",
    "the 'ready' rows here, and it rings the pill red on the ones whose",
    "'failed' is true.",
    "",
    "Five kinds. 'ready' is still to send (never asked, a failed send, or a",
    "delivery the handset never got). 'sent' is a delivery not known to have",
    "failed. 'open' is opened/part-answered and outranks a missing number.",
    "'nophone' has no usable mobile. 'done' is the completed form and outranks",
    "everything. 'failed' is the finer reading over the SAME record: true when",
    "the last attempt was rejected or bounced, so a to-send row is a failure",
    "(red) rather than merely pending (grey). Each case is",
    "preSmsState(stay, pre, invite, fix, spa) and preSmsFailed(invite)."
  ],

  "cases": [
